Pinned one release family behind vendor/gridfinity-rebuilt-openscad-910e22d8
(2.0.0) because that release does not draw the side and back walls of its
spiral-vase bins (upstream issue #340, "Walls not generating in
gridfinity-spiral-vase.scad", still open; its 2.0.0 migration dropped the
full-height wall profile that v1's block_wall swept). This revision is the last
1.x state of the generator, renders a complete vase bin, and matches the
parameter set the Gridfinity Rebuilt web generator exposes. Only the vase-file
object (gridfinity_vase_bin) uses this tree; everything else stays on 2.0.0.

All OpenSCAD sources (the four top-level library files, src/core, src/helpers
and the bundled src/external/threads-scad), the upstream LICENSE and its
README.md, copied verbatim from the pinned commit.

